WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.628 --> 00:00:02.328
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you do, Ollie?

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:09.770
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> I work in digital marketing, I do the social media for different companies on Facebook, Instagram, and Google.

3
00:00:10.106 --> 00:00:13.092
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What about Andrew? What does he do?

4
00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:16.339
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> He works for a publishing company. He’s an editor.

5
00:00:16.722 --> 00:00:19.110
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Where in the house do you work?

6
00:00:19.325 --> 00:00:21.959
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> I work at the kitchen table most of the time.

7
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:29.110
Andrew’s in the office two days a week, but normally he sits opposite me. We live in a very small flat!

8
00:00:29.201 --> 00:00:31.315
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you work long hours?

9
00:00:31.452 --> 00:00:38.466
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> Not really. I start at about 10.00, when I get back from the gym, and I finish at about 6.00.

10
00:00:38.573 --> 00:00:42.095
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> And Andrew? Does he work long hours?

11
00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:48.756
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> He also works from 10.00 until 6.00, but sometimes he works in the evenings when he’s really busy.

12
00:00:48.909 --> 00:00:52.844
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you think are the pros and cons of working from home?

13
00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:59.490
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> The good thing is that I don’t need to travel to work. That’s fantastic. And we have lunch together.

14
00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:04.941
The bad thing is that sometimes we need to make phone calls or have meetings,

15
00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:09.336
so one of us needs to go to the bedroom, and it’s a very small bedroom.

16
00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:14.543
And I miss chatting to people at work, and going to the pub with them after work.

17
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:18.754
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have tips for other people who work from home together?

18
00:01:20.025 --> 00:01:24.236
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> Tell the other person when you have meetings or phone calls.

19
00:01:25.124 --> 00:01:28.875
Work in another space for some of the week, if possible.

20
00:01:28.967 --> 00:01:33.959
Don’t sit in the same place all day – stand up and move, make coffee.

21
00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:42.366
Stop work for lunch, and turn off your computer. And it helps if you like the same music!